  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset suggests a potential relationship between Estropipate and Cyp2c9, mediated through Estrone. Estropipate is linked to several clinical conditions, including Superficial Phlebothrombosis, Abnormal Withdrawal Bleeding, and Retinal Vascular Thrombosis, all of which are caused by Estrone. Estrone binds to Cyp2c9, indicating a possible enzymatic interaction that could influence the metabolism of substrates. The shared pathway involving Estrone and Cyp2c9 across multiple paths highlights a consistent mechanism where Estrone acts as a bridge between Estropipate and the enzyme Cyp2c9. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is supported by multiple independent connections, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between Estropipate and Cyp2c9 through Estrone.",
